            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The air tightness of the house needs to be increased. A lot of air infiltrate inside the house through the bathroom exhausting fans and from the windows. Also, the basement, at the moment of our inspection we noticed a big gap between the interior temperatures. The mechanical room seems to be the main source of the air infiltration in the basement.</airSeal>
                <windows>The windows need to be replaced. The wood frame was damaged by the condensation problem and the seal inside the windows doesn?????????t seems to be working anymore. In fact, we noticed air infiltration around the unit coming from the glass and not from the frame. This could be a sign that the seals of the windows are not working anymore. We recommend the replacement of the windows by ENERGY STAR certified units suited for the northern climate. Please consult a windows specialist for more details to obtain the right product.</windows>
                <doors>At the moment of the energy audit, we noticed that the doors are also another source of air infiltration. The weather strips of the main entrance door need to be replaced. The framing of the basement back door seems to be badly installed and the exterior light is visible through the edges of the door. Weather strips or sealant must be installed to ensure a better airtightness of the door.

We recommend the replacement of the doors by ENERGY STAR certified units suited for northern climate.

</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>The condensation on the windows can be an indicator of a high level of humidity inside the house. The installation of a ventilation unit might help to reduce the level of humidity and reduce the chances of condensation on the windows. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilation) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) certified and ENERGY STAR certified. The installation of such equipment will regulate the air quality of the house and ensuring a proper ventilation. </VentilationSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>We recommend the installation of a hygrometer to monitor the level of humidity inside the house. 

HEATING SYSTEM: During the inspection the client mention the idea of changing heating system since he needs to change the oil tank according the new regulation of the city of Whitehorse. Since the oil furnace is not very old it might be better to keep it and investing in changing the oil storage tank. Changing the system might be very expensive and not necessarily efficient if the airtightness is not fixed.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
